ion the next  time they go to use that attack and fail  so now they've got to go back to the  drawing board reinvest in some cases  they begin to aggregate themselves and  become a much bigger signature a much  bigger target and the international  community has a much better chance of  actually seeing them what does your cost  curve look like well how much do you  have to but what's the average age of a  person that comes and interviews for a  job with your business and what's the  cut of inflation rate in wages that  you're having to pay yeah well the  Christian flate rate is high because it  right now there's a there's a lack of  supply of trained and experienced cyber  professionals so they can they can  command you know much much higher  salaries I think from from an age  distribution it varies we were talking  previously that you know in the past  we'd have to go back and higher kind of  the young hackers sort of speaking up  refer to them as black hats I don't  think that's true any longer I mean is  it the universities and corporations are  really producing some some high quality  cyber talent and so now we're seeing a  range of yes in some cases young you  know out of school but I think there's a  lot of good experience people that maybe  had some government experience or have  been in the corporate world for 10 to 20  years that really are extremely valuable  so that that that kind of dynamic is  changing a little bit problem is though  we still have a deficit in trained  security professionals and so we're all  competing pretty aggressively for the  best of the best

